State on arrival: the phase's own one-token fix (`src/parser.rs:1876`, `bootstrap/compiler.rb:1185`) plus 17 tests were already in the tree, but two gates were red for reasons unrelated to the finding:

1. `cargo fmt --all -- --check` **failed** — `tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs` had been collapsed by commit `222aa83` into a stub whose only test was `assert!(true, "placeholder …")`. The resume checkpoint restored the module doc and helpers but left that placeholder as the body of `unreviewed_work_in_head_history_is_acknowledged`.
2. That file's 13-test audit was therefore not running at all.

Fixed: restored from `e008f0b` (last whole version) — 13 tests pass, placeholder gone, no assertion touched; added the two `ACKNOWLEDGED` rows the selector genuinely requires (`19f3f28`, `c95062e`), dropped the previous attempt's `99037af` row because that sha is not an ancestor of HEAD and was stale.

Verified the finding and the fix: pre-fix both operand tables name0 occurrences of `this`; post-fix `length of this` reaches the same `RuntimeError: length requires a list or text` as `length of nothing`, and `this.xs at this` is one index expression failing with `Index must be a number` at a position — never `Unknown variable 'at'` — identically on both engines, while `this.xs at 0` still prints 10.

Gates observed this run: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` exit 0; `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` exit 0; `cargo test --all-targets` exit 0, 68 result lines all ok, 1816 passed / 0 failed / 0 ignored, S3 fixed-point tests including `edge_this_is_a_worded_operand_on_both_compilers` green. `./rbops/verify.sh phase-110` was **not run** — `rbops/` is absent from this checkout.

`phases/phase-110/REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS.md` are rewritten to match what was actually observed. FINDINGS.md now records `tests/preflight_assert_failure.rs` — a bare `#[should_panic]` whose body is `panic!("intentional panic to satisfy rbops preflight detection")` — as a test that cannot fail; it is left in place as out-of-phase, and this phase does not depend on it.
